From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: blurbery <271863866+blurbery@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ao_avfoundation: decoded PCM sink with a bounded tvOS mode

Adds ao_avfoundation_pcm.h and .c, the decisions of the output's decoded
PCM sink. Patch 0016 binds them to AVSampleBufferAudioRenderer and
AVSampleBufferRenderSynchronizer.

On iOS, and on tvOS while ao-avfoundation-max-lookahead is 0, the sink
behaves as upstream's: 100 ms reads driven by readiness callbacks, the
renderer's end time handed to mpv as its audio clock, and a restart on
WasFlushedAutomatically and OutputConfigurationDidChange. The only change
is a "trace edge reset" line at every reset.

On tvOS with max-lookahead above 0 (Vivid sets 4 on AirPlay routes), the
renderer queue is bounded to the larger of max-lookahead and audio-buffer
and filled from a 50 ms timer, with up to four reads per tick, each behind
the prefetch guard, so volume changes are heard promptly. Every reset
installs a new renderer and synchroniser at the next start, carrying the
volume and mute across and moving the restart observers to the new
renderer; notifications from a replaced renderer are ignored. This mode
logs trace edges, a periodic "pcm:" transport line and the fresh-sink,
renderer-failure and restart lines Vivid reads, and asks for an audio
reload when the renderer fails or cannot be replaced.

Licence: this patch is part of Vivid's Lucid Engine patch series for mpv.
Like the mpv files it adds or changes, it is free software; you can
